entries.description:
WHAT IS CACHED IS WHAT A FUNCTION RETURNS. `Cached` after the parameter list keeps the answer per combination of argument values: the first call with a combination runs the body, every later call with the same values gets the kept answer without entering the function. That is the whole point, which is why only a Function can be Cached - a Procedure returns nothing, and the modifier is refused there.

WHEN TO WRITE IT - the same value is asked for again and again, and the answer depends on the arguments only:
- the accounting policy for a period, asked for every line of every document;
- settings and switches;
- a rate for (currency, date);
- anything worked out from metadata.
A loop over ten thousand rows asking `InventoryMethod(period)` reads the register once per period, not ten thousand times. So whenever code reads the same setting or policy in more than one place, or inside a loop, the reading goes into a Cached function and every caller simply asks it.

IT MAY RETURN ANYTHING, and the answer lives AS LONG AS ITS OWNER - there is nothing to clear and no timer:
- a common module: the whole session;
- an object module: while that object lives;
- a form module: while the form is open.
Every caller with the same arguments gets the SAME value - a returned structure or table is one object for all of them.

NOT FOR:
- a function with side effects: the second call does not run;
- an answer that depends on something besides the arguments (the current date, data written since): it is seen again only when the owner is gone - for a common module, the next session.

Arguments are compared BY VALUE: the number 1 and the string "1" are different keys. A call that raised is not kept.

entries.example:
// the policy for a period: read once per period, however often it is asked -
// in a common module, for the whole session
Function InventoryMethod(Date period) Public Cached
{
    Return ReadPolicy(period);
}

Function ReadPolicy(Date period) Private
{
    If (period < Date(2026, 1, 1)) { Return "Average"; }
    Return "FIFO";
}

// the caller just asks, as often as it needs
var method = "";
for (i = 1 To 1000) {
    method = InventoryMethod(Date(2026, 3, 1));   // the body ran once
}

